.idea/
target/
.vscode/
.venv/
# Personal, machine-specific paths. These were generated by a setup script for the docs worktree
# scheme, which was dropped on 2026-08-16 along with the script; the files it left behind are still
# in working trees, so the rule stays.
*.code-workspace
# Running examples/config_builder.py leaves examples/__pycache__/ behind, which
# showed up as untracked for whoever ran it. Byte-code, never shared.
__pycache__/
# The legacy C++ is TRACKED, in legacy/. It used to be ignored at the repo root, which meant the
# implementation the Rust is ported from lived on one laptop — and a doc comment citing it pointed
# at a file nobody else had. It is reference, not a build target; see legacy/README.md.
handoff_transfer_from_c++.md
handoff_edge_multiplicity_cap_simplification.md
**/target/

# SUPERSEDED 2026-08-16 by the blanket `.claude/` below. This block used to explain which parts of
# `.claude/` were tracked here and why `work/<owner>/current/` stopped being ignored on 2026-08-13.
# None of that is this file's business any more: GET tracks nothing under `.claude/`, so what is
# tracked, ignored or pushed inside it is decided by GET-claude's own `.gitignore`, which already
# carries the `settings.local.json` rule this block ended with. The reasoning itself is not lost —
# it lives in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` under "Working docs" and in `decisions.md`.

# .claude/ is its own repository now - md12ol/GET-claude, cloned as this directory.
# Agreed at the joint meeting of 2026-08-13 (GitHub #74). Keeping it out of GET is what
# keeps it out of every clone, every release branch and the built wheel.
.claude/

# Output of the get-run dev CLI (see get/src/bin/run.rs), written into whatever directory it
# is run from. Generated per run, never shared.
run_log.csv
best_individual.txt
best_individual.txt.toml
